pure-line-room
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes software developed by Animnia as part of pure-line-room
(https://github.com/Animnia/pure-line-room), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Taken from that work and still recognisable here:

  the room geometry and the line/fill drawing helpers — black 1px edges over
    white fills pushed back by a polygon offset, which is what makes the whole
    scene read as a single pen drawing with no lighting and no shading
  the renderer setup, hover bolding via fat lines, and picking
  the day/night palette inversion
  the Web Audio synthesis

Changed in this fork:

  every object became a device with an ABSOLUTE setter rather than a
    click-toggle, so "turn the lamp off" is a no-op when the lamp is already
    off — language is idempotent in a way a mouse click is not
  a scene-agnostic stage, registry, parser and worker sit under the room, so
    the schema experiments could be run against more than one scene
  the room was refitted as a smart home and given a tool schema
  the six recorded sound samples were dropped in favour of the synthesized
    fallbacks that already existed beside them

